sted Peer Review at Scale: The AAAI-26 AI Review Pilot\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2604.13940\"},{\"title\":\"Technical Paper Recommendation: A Study in Combining Multiple   Information Sources\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1106.0248\"}]\n\nLet me search for the actual AAAI-26 reviewer form or guidelines with the specific rating scale.\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"AAAI-26 Review Process - AAAI\",\"url\":\"https://aaai.org/conference/aaai/aaai-26/review-process/\"},{\"title\":\"Instructions for AAAI-26 Reviewers - AAAI\",\"url\":\"https://aaai.org/conference/aaai/aaai-26/instructions-for-aaai-26-reviewers/\"},{\"title\":\"AAAI-26 Review Process Update: Scale, Integrity Measures, and Pathways to Sustainability - AAAI\",\"url\":\"https://aaai.org/conference/aaai/aaai-26/review-process-update/\"},{\"title\":\"Are reviewers suggested by authors as good as those chosen by editors? Results of a rater-blinded, retrospective study\",\"url\":\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC1482713/\"},{\"title\":\"Ethical Guidelines for AAAI-26 Reviewers - AAAI\",\"url\":\"https://aaai.org/conference/aaai/aaai-26/ethical-guidelines-for-aaai-26-reviewers/\"},{\"title\":\"Substantial Agreement of Referee Recommendations at a General Medical Journal – A Peer Review Evaluation at Deutsches Ärzteblatt International\",\"url\":\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC3642182/\"},{\"title\":\"On the determinants of journal rejection rates: evidence from the Journal of Financial Economics\",\"url\":\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC12868043/\"},{\"title\":\"AAAI-26 FAQ for Authors (Rebuttal) - AAAI\",\"url\":\"https://aaai.org/conference/aaai/aaai-26/aaai-26-faq-for-authors-rebuttal/\"},{\"title\":\"Examining uncertainty in journal peer reviewers’ recommendations: a cross-sectional study\",\"url\":\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC11387066/\"}]\n\nLet me try one more specific search for the actual AAAI-26 reviewer rating scale document.\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"AAAI-26 Review Process Update: Scale, Integrity Measures, and Pathways to Sustainability - AAAI\",\"url\":\"https://aaai.org/conference/aaai/aaai-26/review-process-update/\"},{\"title\":\"AAAI Launches AI-Powered Peer Review Assessment System - AAAI\",\"url\":\"https://aaai.org/aaai-launches-ai-powered-peer-review-assessment-system/\"},{\"title\":\"Main Technical Track: Call for Papers - AAAI\",\"url\":\"https://aaai.org/conference/aaai/aaai-26/main-technical-track-call/\"},{\"title\":\"Instructions for AAAI-26 Reviewers - AAAI\",\"url\":\"https://aaai.org/conference/aaai/aaai-26/instructions-for-aaai-26-reviewers/\"},{\"title\":\"AAAI-26 Review Process - AAAI\",\"url\":\"https://aaai.org/conference/aaai/aaai-26/review-process/\"}]\n\nBased on my web search results, I found information about the AAAI-26 reviewer process, though the specific 1-10 numerical rating scale you mentioned in your query is not directly detailed in the search results I retrieved.\n\nHere's what I found about AAAI-26 reviewer instructions:\n\n## AAAI-26 Review Process Overview\n\nAAAI-26 follows a two-phase reviewing process with two additions: an additional AI-generated review in Phase 1, and an AI-generated summary of the discussions at the end of the discussion phase.\n\n## Recommendation System\n\nOnly the human reviews will have a paper rating and recommendations — the AI-generated reviews will not have any ratings or recommendations. Recommendations are not made by averaging the reviewers' scores. Paper recommendations are made by senior members after considering all available information, including the reviews, the scores, the author response, and the reviewer discussions.\n\n## Evaluation Structure\n\nEvery paper is allocated three reviewers. If a paper receives sufficiently negative reviews, it will be rejected without any opportunity for author feedback. Remaining papers will progress to Phase 2.\n\nUnfortunately, the search results do not contain the specific details ab